MYSQL Capstone Project 2
Hospital Management System 
  
1) Database Design
This project is a Hospital Management System built using MySQL. 
It manages the complete flow of hospital operations — patients, doctors, appointments, treatments, billing, and payments — using 7 tables:
•	patients — stores patient name, city, gender, age, and phone number
•	doctors — stores doctor name, specialization, department, and consultation fee
•	departments — stores department names like Cardiology, Neurology, and Orthopedics
•	appointments — stores appointment date and status for each patient and doctor
•	treatments — stores individual treatment name and cost for each appointment
•	bills — stores bill date, total amount, and bill status for each appointment
•	payments — stores payment mode, paid amount, and payment status for each bill

2) Table Relationships
•	departments → doctors — One department can have many doctors (One-to-Many)
•	patients → appointments — One patient can have many appointments (One-to-Many)
•	doctors → appointments — One doctor can handle many appointments (One-to-Many)
•	appointments → treatments — One appointment has one treatment (One-to-One)
•	appointments → bills — One appointment generates one bill (One-to-One)
•	patients → bills — One patient can have many bills (One-to-Many)
•	bills → payments — One bill has one payment (One-to-One)

3) Key Insights from Reports
•	Chennai has the most patients (4 out of 12)
•	Bypass Surgery is the highest cost treatment at ₹20,000
•	UPI and Cash are the most preferred payment methods
•	11 out of 20 appointments were successfully completed
•	2 cancelled appointments still have associated bills needing correction
•	Patients like Aarav Sharma visited multiple times showing recurring healthcare needs
•	Doctor Ramesh Kumar handled the highest number of appointments

4) Summary
This Hospital Management System covers the complete hospital workflow using 7 well connected tables. 
The project includes 52 SQL queries covering filtering, aggregation, joins, subqueries, group by, and data quality checks — making it a complete and practical database project.

•	Bills 12 and 13 have no payments and need immediate follow-up for revenue recovery
•	Data quality checks revealed invalid foreign keys in appointments 19 and 20
